WEBVTT

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.170
When did he?

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.390
Robert Horton.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:46.060
A mafia heavyweight who's been rapidly
expanding his influence on Wall Street recently.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.020
If we don't act,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.570
he's sure to use his organization's power to
disrupt market conditions not only in America,

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:58.160
but throughout the entire world for his own advantage.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.500
We at the SEC have held a number of meetings to determine how to best deal with this problem,

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.080
and the final outcome of the discussion was...

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.080
So we're unanimous, then.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.470
We decided that the only way to protect the world's financial markets is to eliminate him.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.550
The reward is three million dollars.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.140
Well, Mr. Golgo 13?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.310
Where can I find the target?

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.940
Horton is a cautious man.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.020
He'll never show an opening when he's out in the city.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.030
The only place to get him is when he's in his office on 7th Avenue.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.110
But...

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.820
That office is, well...

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.910
It's the 31st floor of the Harrison Building.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.960
It's 300 feet off the ground.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:19.280
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:30.630
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:42.390
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:48.690
The weak person I was is no more

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:54.270
I decided to just believe

00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:01.410
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.240
I go towards you

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.960
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.090
I go towards you

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:21.130
Blown by the wind

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:26.600
Oh blown

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.820
I've told you not to loiter around here before.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.030
Gimmie a break, Charlie!

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.990
Wait!

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.780
Hey!

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.460
Get started.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.170
Carol!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.390
Measure the distance from the floor to that point and the final place the bullet ended up.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.970
Accurately.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.100
I'll take care of it, Sam.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:34.980
Eddy...

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.400
Calmed down a bit?

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.150
I apologize for being hysterical.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.190
It's understandable.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.610
However, Miss Peggy,

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.910
as a police officer I need to hear your story in order to catch the guy who did this.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.030
I understand.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.870
Mr. Horton had just returned from Europe.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.960
Was that in his itinerary?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:58.710
Yes.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:03.920
He came here directly from the airport and arrived here around five o'clock, just as his itinerary said.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.170
What was the precise time he came in?

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.760
Just around five.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:11.220
And?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.260
As soon as he came in,

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.850
Mr. Horton asked me to raise the blinds.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:19.940
This is a southern facing window, so we leave them down during the day,

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.730
but Mr. Horton loved to see the sun set on the city.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.820
And the second I finished raising the blinds...

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.160
It's not your fault, Peggy.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.080
This was the work of a professional.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:44.300
He made his plan based off a thorough analysis of the target's movements and habits.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:49.800
And he made it with one shot, at sunset, when it's easy to miss.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.390
I'm not even sure where to start looking for clues.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.600
He could've shot from any one of those buildings.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.270
We can narrow it down.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:06.230
Based off the direction the bullet traveled, it's either the Fiver Building or the Electrical Central Building.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.150
From the roof of either one of those places?

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.620
It would be about 100 meters from the Fiver Building,

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.200
and 200 or so from Electric Central,

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.410
but neither of those are out of the question for a talented sniper.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.580
This is the height from the floor of both of those points.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.000
Good timing.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:28.420
If we know the vertical angle, we can find which roof he shot from.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.010
Are you sure about this?

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.010
Of course, I was careful, Sam.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.010
What's wrong?

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:38.680
The bullet hole in the window is one hundred and seventy centimeters from the floor.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.850
The bullet went through the victim's head

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:45.020
and embedded itself in the wall at a height of 173 centimeters.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.230
Which means?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.240
The bullet came in at an angle slightly above the horizontal.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.570
In other words, it was fired from somewhere lower than this room.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.870
But the roofs of both of those buildings are higher than this room.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.040
It wasn't shot from the roof.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.380
But neither of those buildings have windows.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.880
A gondola?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.800
Maybe at night,

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.840
but he'd stand out too much during the day.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:14.300
So where'd the bastard fire from, then?

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:21.980
Detective.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.730
Charlie found this during his patrol.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:33.150
36 caliber long rifle rimfire ammo.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.990
It was 5 PM when he picked it up, just about the time when Horton was assassinated.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.000
When I picked it up the case was still warm,

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.000
like it had just been fired.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.710
Where did you pick it up?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:52.720
Here.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.260
In an alley in front of East McGregor Apartments.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.810
I don't think it's got anything to do with the case, Sam.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.480
There's more than 500 meters between this point and 7th Avenue.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.480
It basically matches the direction of the bullet, but...

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.570
I can see it.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.200
But Sam, it's over 500 meters away!

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.120
Carol!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:21.490
Yes sir.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.040
Take this to forensics.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.250
Now.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.000
Yes sir.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.710
Let's go, Eddy.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.420
Are you serious?

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:31.340
Hey.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.340
Let's say, hypothetically, that that round was fired by our sniper.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:43.560
Why does he have to pick a spot that's 500 meters away?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:49.270
There are a lot of other places closer.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.530
A professional is going to choose the place with the highest possibility of success.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.360
Normally, yes.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.160
And even if he is our guy,

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.120
we're not going to find anything.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.870
He pulled off his job. He's probably long gone.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.380
Even so, as long as we can get some clue as to who he is...

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.000
I'm gonna catch this guy.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.720
This place is 30 stories tall,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.560
but from the angle of the bullet, we can rule out any place lower than the 25th floor.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.770
Damn it, I hate this wind.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.020
It's been blowing like this since morning!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.900
Damn, it's cold.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.950
A southern wind...

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.280
It'd be a tailwind, but just in case...

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:45.330
It's me, Frank.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:50.250
Get the weather people on the phone and find the weather conditions from 5 PM today.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.210
I need details.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.050
A suspicious person?

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.930
We've got 909 rooms here.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.140
What kind of person was this?

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.930
Mr. Tougou in Room 909, the last room.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.140
From the name, he sounds like a Japanese guy.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:13.150
He was probably an athlete, a really tough guy.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:16.190
He rented the room three days ago.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.530
He signed a short term contract for only a week.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:25.160
And there are other open rooms on the 30th floor, 907 and 908,

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.950
but he chose the most inconvenient one, the one on the end furthest from the elevator.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.410
Why?

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.040
I don't know.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:34.420
He's the one who chose it.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.420
Is he still here?

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.380
Sometimes our tenants just up and vanish.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.180
But it's not like I care, in his case.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:48.020
He paid his week's rent in advance.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:11.960
Who's there?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.120
The Police.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.000
Open up.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.300
Mr. Tougou, yes?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.470
I'm Sam Shayand from the NYPD.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.510
Eddy Morgan.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.140
We're wasting our time, Sam.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:32.390
A sniper who pulled off his job wouldn't stay here.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.810
Let us in.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.310
There are some things we'd like to ask you.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:35.940
Sam.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.690
I'm sure of it.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.570
He's our man.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.300
You're leaving?

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.300
Your contract was for a week.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.800
Something came up.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.810
It's not 'cause your work here is done?

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.370
Why did you pick the room on the very edge?

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.580
It's close to the emergency stairway.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.120
I've been in hotel fires before, in Cairo and Hamburg.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.760
I looked in the back, but there was nothing suspicious.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.400
We're going to take a look around your room.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.360
Sam?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.660
It's me.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.450
Send some men over.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.200
Now.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.920
We should find something.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.640
I know it.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:32.600
Something.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:48.070
I don't know what you're after, but could you hurry?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.660
I won't catch my plane.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.710
I looked in the other empty rooms.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.050
I checked the one below us too, of course.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.800
There's nothing, Sam.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.720
We've looked everywhere and found nothing.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.390
I guess you're done.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.350
The dust chute!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:24.230
Check the garbage dumpster below!

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.270
Yes sir.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:38.500
Were you in Cairo and Hamburg on business, Tougou?

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:50.470
The bullet extracted from the wall of the crime scene was a 36 magnum round,

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:53.390
which is a fairly unusual round with nickel steel coating.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:57.010
Some Weatherby rifles use them.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:01.440
So the gun used in the shooting could be a Weatherby rifle then, for instance?

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.770
From the depth it embedded itself in the wall,

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:13.280
we can assume that it was fired from a distance of 200 to 600 meters.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:19.040
So this place, 500 meters away, is within that range.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.040
What about that case?

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.920
We didn't find any fingerprints.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:29.550
But it's quite possible that the bullet and case will match.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.550
We've connected it after all, then,

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:37.100
Horton's shooting and that case.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.970
We found it, Sam.

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:43.850
A Weatherby.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.560
Magnum Mark 5.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.360
Hello?

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:47.480
Hello, Sam?

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.730
Good timing.

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:50.940
Thanks, Carol.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:52.950
Tougou.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.910
You're going to have to cancel your flight.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.610
Why?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:02.200
Somebody hired you to do your work with this rifle,

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:07.330
and after you were done with it, you threw it in that dust chute.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:18.220
Do you have any proof that that's my rifle?

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:22.520
I don't think we'll find your fingerprints on it.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.480
But I can tell.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:30.400
I've met thousands of lowlife criminals, so my intuition's pretty good.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.730
From this room,

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.290
you took Horton's life.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.250
What's wrong, Sam?

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.560
It's too far!

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:08.400
You can only barely see the Harrison building in between the gaps of the other buildings.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:16.950
You couldn't possibly hit someone on the other side of a window.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.870
No, you could.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:26.000
Even at the long range distance of 500 meters,

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.120
even at dusk when it's easy to miss your shot,

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.750
you can hit a man in the head with a single shot.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:37.970
You're a Super-A class sniper who could pull off such an impossible shot.

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:38.880
Sam...

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:48.770
You borrowed this room three days ago to match Horton's return to this country!

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:52.400
You didn't choose this room because it was near the emergency stairs.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:57.690
It's because this is the only place you can get a straight look into Horton's office,

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:00.410
room 909!

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.700
You're coming with us, Tougou.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:09.460
We're going to interrogate you at HQ.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.630
I don't have time to waste on that.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.250
Shut up!

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.340
I'll drag your ass there myself!

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:15.710
Detective.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:18.130
What's wrong, Frank?

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:22.470
I looked up what you asked me to with the airport's weather people.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:26.310
The weather conditions for this area around 5 o'clock.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:27.310
And then...

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.100
Temperature of 14 degrees.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.810
Humidity of 34%.

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.940
Eastern wind at a speed of 6.2 meters.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.230
An eastern wind?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.320
You mean a southern wind, right?

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.400
It's a southern wind now.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.360
But the direction of the wind changed at about 5:30.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:44.120
An eastern wind had been blowing the rest of the day.

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.540
Maybe with a tailwind, when the wind was southern,

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:54.290
but nobody could pull that shot off
with a sidewind blowing to the east.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:01.760
It's impossible, yeah.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.800
May I go?

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.220
It's time.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.490
I'm sure he's the one who killed Horton.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.580
It's him, Tougou.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:36.040
But you said it was impossible...

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:40.460
I said it's impossible to find him guilty even if we arrested him.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:43.590
The distance of 500 meters,

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.260
the time,

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.850
sunset, and a sidewind blowing east.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:55.400
Who'd believe that there's a sniper who could pull off a shot even with those horrible conditions?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:01.490
I can tell you what the judge would say even if we sent it to trial.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.070
Not guilty!

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:09.330
Innocent!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.580
Sam...

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:18.540
Why did he stay here even after he finished his job?

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:21.090
I know the answer now.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:24.090
There was no need to rush away.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:29.600
The instant he chose this incredibly far away spot to make his shot from,

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:33.180
he eliminated himself from the pool of suspects.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:38.100
To prove that he was the one who fired the gun,

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.860
you'd have to prove that there was a monster who walked among us with the skills of a god.

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:49.620
But that's impossible.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.200
In other words...

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:55.870
Nobody can convict him.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:05.720
But...

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:11.140
If we had a witness, things would be different.

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:49.550
Chiisana koto ni zenryoku ni naru kimi no sugata yuuki ni natta hibi

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:49.550
Those days I saw you giving your all for small things filled me with courage

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:57.020
Zutto horyuu shippanashi jya ugokenai

00:22:49.550 --> 00:22:57.020
If I keep them suspended then I won't be able to move

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:06.570
GARASU no HAIWEI ni tatteiru you ni

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:06.570
It's like I'm standing on a glass highway

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:13.780
Yume to kiken to senaka awase demo

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:13.780
Even if I'm standing back to back with dreams and danger

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.920
Kono nagai michi wo sukoshizutsu arukou

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.920
I'll take this long road one step at a time

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:27.090
Soshite kimi wa ano koro mitai ni

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:27.090
And I need you to smile

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:30.090
Waratteite

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:30.090
Like you did back then

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:36.720
Shiokaze ni yurete sasayakiatta

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:36.720
It shook in the sea breeze and whispered

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:47.320
Kagayaiteita tooi ano hi wa kagerou

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:47.320
That distant and shining day is a shimmering haze

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:49.190
The shining days

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:55.160
Tsumaranai koto ni makeru ni wa hayasugiru

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:55.160
I can't lose to something so trivial

00:24:01.250 --> 00:24:04.330
Gunshots ring out amidst the heat of the desert.

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:06.500
A sudden attack has begun;

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:10.010
it was a trap set for Golgo.

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:13.930
The enemy's plan is to sell a new rifle.

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:18.600
A battle begins between the strongest brothers and Golgo!

00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:21.430
Next time on Golgo 13:

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:26.940
The Masterpiece Assault Rifle

00:24:21.430 --> 00:24:24.230
Masterpiece Assault Rifle

00:24:24.230 --> 00:24:28.070
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
